        "date": "2026-11-21T11:48:16Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(tools,app): cutting data for wood, MDF, plywood, acrylic and HDPE\n\nAdd six router work materials (softwood, hardwood, mdf, plywood,\nacrylic, hdpe) to the milling and turning tables. Their chip load\nfollows a router curve by cutter diameter (cutting_router), so a small\ncutter gets a thin chip. On a router material a V-bit reads its chip\nload at half its diameter. The existing machine rpm clamp recomputes\nthe feed at the clamped rpm and names the clamp.\n\nFixes #3068\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
